From c69b53538f8a7b6695f9ad37cd3094ee69271349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:53:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-76..78: double-click = the default event (created
 when empty), Shift+F7, the outline's right-click menu (0.78.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"改得跟WPF 操作模式一樣" / "所有基礎操作模式能跟WPF一樣方便" (EastSun 20260930),
parts 4-7, each from Microsoft's own wording:
- 0.76.0 "In Design view, double-click the control ... The default event
  handler for the control is created. The code-behind file is opened": a
  double-click on a component = its default event (BCB6's: OnClick; OnChange
  for edits / combos / track bars / page controls; OnTimer; the form OnCreate
  -- vclevents.defaultEventOf) -- its code when set, created and wired (the
  same as the events table) when empty. F7 / View Code and Enter on the design
  surface only open code (the default event's, else the form's .cpp), never
  add one.
- 0.77.0 Shift+F7 (WPF: between Design and XAML): in the designer = the
  selected component's HTML; in a page's HTML = its designer with the element
  at the cursor (in its tag or its text) selected; in C++ = showCodeInDesigner.
  The design surface's help line says the new keys.
- 0.78.0 "Right-click the element in the Document Outline window or the
  artboard": the component tree's right-click menu has the design surface's
  commands (cut / copy / paste / delete / rename, view code, HTML / DFM, Order,
  Group Into, Ungroup, reset to DFM, hide / lock in design); the row's
  component is selected first (onNode).
- reset to DFM right after a move: position / size are read from the SOURCE (the move is in it) -- the page, not drawn again yet, still showed the old place and the reset found 1 item of 2 (seen in the real VS Code test on a busy machine).
- vscode_it: the reset-to-DFM step waits for the page to report the move
  (a busy machine redrew after the reset had measured, 1 item instead of 2);
  select-same-type waits 10 s.

Tests (all 4 layers pass): lib (defaultEventOf), probe (Enter posts a
view-only double-click), smoke (Label1 double-click -> Label1Click created and
wired, F7 on Label2 only opens fHotPlate.cpp; the element at the cursor; Copy
from the Panel2 row copies Panel2; the outline menu has the commands), real VS
Code (Shift+F7 from the page's HTML selects spbSave in the designer).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
